        "original_id": "128dc182-fba8-5961-8de1-f795e6b8cb98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Pomona College, Brown University, Claremont Colleges consortium\n- People: David W. Oxtoby, Charles P. Nott\n- Places: Providence, Rhode Island, United States\n- Roles: college president, football team captain\n- Topics: higher education, college football\n\nFacts:\n- Brown University was founded in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.\n- Brown University is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\n- Pomona College was established in 1887 and is the founding member of the Claremont Colleges consortium.\n- Charles P. Nott played college football at Brown University and was the captain of the Brown Bears football team in 1895.\n- David W. Oxtoby is an American academic who served as the ninth president of Pomona College.\n- Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.",
